3. Can truncation explain the steepening?

   measured steepening (last minus first log-step): +0.2410
   after correcting every size for its deficit:     +0.2052
   share of the steepening explained by truncation: +14.9%

   Deficits enter every log-step almost equally, so they shift the reach
   level without bending it. Truncation changes what the absolute reach
   means; it does not manufacture the curvature.
